    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. regarding the interlocking part, do you have a specific pattern you'd recommend? also we have some uneven loads sometimes that make the stack feel a bit \"unpredictable\" or like they might shift suddenly even when they look okay. any tips on how to spot that before it's too late?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For interlocking, patterns such as triangle, square, or herringbone positioning can enhance stability. As for unequal loads, consistently checking stack weight distribution, considering installing rack toe supports, reinforcing pallet ends, and regularly inspecting for damage are essential practices in preemptively identifying any instability. Additionally, marking weight limit stickers on the racking and storing heavy loads centrally can prevent unforeseen shifting. Regular staff training on these precautions is also important.",
      "source": "target",
